---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Tildes from '../components/Tildes.astro';

// The only facts on this page that change. Keep them here.
const terms = {
  prototypeFrom: 'US$ 1,500',
  reply: '2 working days',
};

const hello = encodeURIComponent("Hi Fabio, I saw your site. I'd like help with: ");
const wa = `https://wa.me/5511971058388?text=${hello}`;
const mail = `mailto:nunseik@gmail.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Project idea')}`;
---
<Base title="Work with me" file="~/work.md" description="Freelance work for small businesses and startups: automations, bots, websites, apps, AI setup and working prototypes.">
  <div class="buf">
    <h1>work with me</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Yes, I take freelance work.</strong> I help small businesses and startups turn an
      idea, or a tedious manual task, into software that works. I build it end to end on my own,
      so you talk to the person who writes the code.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={wa}>→ message me on WhatsApp</a> <span class="dim">or</span> <a href={mail}>email me</a>{' '}
      <span class="dim">· I reply within {terms.reply} · Portuguese, English or Spanish · remote, anywhere</span>
    </p>

    <h2>what I can build for you</h2>
    <dl class="kv">
      <dt>automations</dt>
      <dd>
        Stop copying things by hand. Spreadsheets that fill themselves, daily reports, price and
        availability trackers, a bot that answers on Telegram or WhatsApp.
        <span class="dim eg">e.g. <a href="/projects/personal-finances/">a finance bot</a>, <a href="/projects/airbnb-tracker/">a booking tracker</a></span>
      </dd>
      <dt>websites</dt>
      <dd>
        A fast site for your business, or an internal tool your team uses every day: dashboards,
        forms, admin pages.
        <span class="dim eg">e.g. <a href="/projects/habla-mucho/">a platform for teachers</a></span>
      </dd>
      <dt>mobile apps</dt>
      <dd>
        iPhone and Android apps, from the first screen to the app stores.
        <span class="dim eg">e.g. <a href="/projects/sentinel/">a crime-map app</a></span>
      </dd>
      <dt>AI setup</dt>
      <dd>
        Put AI to work on your real tasks: transcribing calls, drafting documents, searching your
        own files, or setting up coding agents for your team, safely.
        <span class="dim eg">e.g. <a href="/projects/audio-recorder/">a session recorder</a>, <a href="/tools/">my AI tooling</a></span>
      </dd>
      <dt>prototypes</dt>
      <dd>
        Got an idea and need to show it to customers or investors? I build a working prototype end
        to end: real screens, real data, something people can actually use.
        <span class="dim eg">e.g. <a href="/projects/voo-livro/">Voo Livro</a>, a book-sharing web app with logins, QR codes
        and a real database, built in <strong>one day</strong></span>
      </dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>how it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Send me a message</strong> on <a href={wa}>WhatsApp</a> or by
        <a href={mail}>email</a>. A few lines is enough: what you do today, what you'd like to
        change, and whether there's a deadline. Screenshots or a voice note help.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>I reply within {terms.reply}</strong> with questions, or a short call if it's
        easier to explain out loud.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You get a written plan:</strong> what I'll build, how long it should take, and the
        price. Nothing starts until you agree.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>I build it in small steps</strong> and show you progress as I go, so you can change
        your mind early, not at the end.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>price</h2>
    <dl class="kv">
      <dt>prototype</dt>
      <dd>
        <strong>from {terms.prototypeFrom}</strong>
        <span class="dim eg">a working app with the core features of your idea, ready to show at
        events, to first customers or to investors</span>
      </dd>
      <dt>anything else</dt>
      <dd>a fixed quote in the written plan</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="dim">
      The prototype package covers logins, the main flows of your idea, a real database and a live
      link you can share. <a href="/projects/voo-livro/">Voo Livro</a> is a good example of the
      size. More features, more polish or an app in the stores costs more, and you see the price
      before anything starts.
    </p>

    <h2>not sure if it's a fit?</h2>
    <p>
      Ask anyway. If it's not something I do well, I'll tell you, and point you to what I'd use
      instead.
    </p>
    <p><a href={wa}>→ WhatsApp +55 11 97105-8388</a> <span class="dim">·</span> <a href={mail}>nunseik@gmail.com</a></p>
    <Tildes n={3} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .eg { display: block; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
</style>
